config BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_SNMPD
	bool "thingino-snmpd"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_JCT
	select BR2_PACKAGE_MINI_SNMPD
	help
	  mini-snmpd, a minimal SNMP daemon for embedded systems, wired
	  into thingino. Lets an NMS (LibreNMS, Zabbix, Observium, Cacti,
	  check_mk, ...) poll the camera for uptime, CPU load, memory,
	  disk usage, network interface counters and hwmon temperature
	  sensors.

	  The daemon itself is built by Buildroot's mini-snmpd package;
	  this option adds the Thingino integration layer (init script,
	  shipped defaults and WebUI plugin) on top of it.

	  Read-only SNMP v1/v2c, optional SNMPv2c traps. No SNMPv3.

	  Configuration lives in the "snmpd" section of
	  /etc/thingino.json; a WebUI page is installed when
	  thingino-webui is enabled. The service ships disabled.

	  https://github.com/troglobit/mini-snmpd
